- Sprint 17 Global Events and Sprint 18 Global Incidents dashboard workflows are implemented; remaining backlog starts with Watchlist and later workflow polish.

- Global Events tab
    - Map is too small
    - Events should have an exact address of the venue (street, city, postcode, country)
    - Map should then take the event locations and plot them on the map
    - Map does not need a legend
    - in the topics in the event detail it should not show the bullet point formatting, same structure but without the bullet point formatting
    - When adding a new event it should be a popup where the user inputs the required/optional fields
        - the required fields should be
            - event name
            - format: in-person or online (drop down menu)
                - when drop down menu option is selected then render a new input that either:
                    - if in-person: location (street, city, postcode, country)
                    - if online: URL link to the event meeting (zoom, teams, webinar etc) this can be optional as events dont always show the meeting URL immediately
            - date and time (should be a date time picker)
            - URL
        - optional fields
            - topics
            - source items
    - events records should be editable by analyst, admin, and governance
    - change the name of "Enrich Target" to "Add to Enrichment Queue" and once pressed it should move the participant of that event to the enrichment queue. still keep the participant in the event detail page and grey out the button

    - in event detail, generated, stale, projection and watermarks should only be visible by the governance reviewer


- Global Incidents tab
    - when rejecting or adding to watchlist an incident in the table it should be removed from the table
    - when adding to watchlist, it should be the company going into the watchlist not the incident itself
    - when an incident is corroborated, the button should then change to "Revert"
    - in global incidents the values in company and evidence column should not show the bullet point just the text, same goes for the data in incident detail page
    - the incidents intelligence should be such that if one cyber attack affects multiple companies, then each company has a seperate entry in the incidents tab (same name different company)
    - remove the open button in the incident detail page (not the global incidents tab)
    - in incident detail the watermarks needs to be well formatted not raw json
    - remove languages from incident detail, it is not necessary
    - in incident detail, generated, stale, projection and watermarks should only be visible by the governance reviewer
    - remove confidence from table
    - incident can only be added to watchlist if corroborated
        - grey out the button and then make it clickable when it has been corroborated
    - when manually adding an incident it should be a popup that allows the user to input the following fields:
        - title
        - companies affected
        - type
        - first observed
        - source items
        - domains
        - attack vector
        - evidence (article url etc)
    - what this should do is that if there are multiple companies/domains mentioned then it creates an entry for each company (with the same title as mentioned before).

- Watchlist tab
    - there should be an open button that gives details on a watch list element similar to event detail and incident detail pages, call it "Watchlist Item"
    - in watchlist item there should also be a button that is called "Find Contact" that uses openSERP so search on google with a google dork like:
        - site:linkedin.com/in ("Head of Cybersecurity" OR "CISO" OR "Chief Information Security Officer" OR "CTO" OR "Chief Technology Officer") "{company name}"
    - in terms of the action button:
        - when enabled it should monitor that particular entry, more specifically:
            - if the type is a company then there should be a system that every hour it uses google news api to monitor:
                - changes in board of directors
                - newly appointed CISO, CTO, CIO, or head of cybersecurity
                - cybersecurity attacks
    - for the owner column, it should be the user (actor) that approved the entry to move from the incident tab to the watchlist
    - in terms of the columns:
        - the name field should be the company
        - we dont need the type column
        - we dont need the key column
        - keep origin incident but only show it to the governance reviewer


- Analyst Review tab
    - improve the fake data because it is confusing, use more realistic data
    - the contact enrichment queue should have some fake data
    - to find the website domain of the contact, use openSERP to to search "{company name} official website" and then pick the first link and normalise is (e.g https://www.apple.com/en -> apple.com)

- Sequence State tab
    - for sequence definitions there should be an option to add multiple sequences. it would be a good idea to have a "Sequence Definitions" button that lands you on a page where you can edit your sequence definitions
    - make the sequence definitions editor more user friendly also
        - must be able to add more steps
        - needs to adapt to other channels not just email
        - when an email needs to be sent as part of the sequence then it can be sent once the user has approved it
        - if the sequence is instead a call or demo (google meet), then this should be coordinated/synced with the meetings tab
    - the sequence state should also have the ability to allow the user to import from the CRM and assign a prospect to a sequence

- Meetings tab
    -in meeting detail tab there should not be visible bullet points
    - for the prep packet add a bit of vertical spacing so its more legible.
